<title>SRI LANKA: Ceylon Grain shares dip 4.8 percent..</title>
<headline>Ceylon Grain shares dip 4.8 percent..</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ceylon Grain Elevators Ltd fell 4.8 percent, or 75 cents, to 14.75 rupees, on volume of 400 shares on Wednesday as retail investors took profits, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The scrip rose from about 14.50 after last week's announcement that its subsidiary Three Acre Farms was going for a 280 million-rupee expansion,&quot; said a broker.</p>
<p>The share is now falling in line with the rest of the market, where small investors are taking profits, he said.</p>
<p>The company is involved in feedmilling and poultry breeding.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
